        <p>COWLEY SCHOOLS, ST. HELENS. New Buildings, £15.000. Endowment, £BOO per annum. Scholarships, £l5O per annum. READMA• TAR : E. j. simpsoN, M.A., form rly Foundation Scholar anti Prizeman Trinity College, Cambridge. HEADIEISTRESS MISS FIFE, B.A. Examination, Newnham College, Cambridge. INext TERM begins TUESDAY, SEPTEMBER lOrit, 1895_ Fees £6 to £8 per aonum. Since the year 1884 about Two Thousand Certificates have been gain-d by pupils in the South Kensington Science and Art Examinations many of these being in the Honours and nearly Five hundred In the Advanced Stages. Very high places have been taken in the Pass and Honours lists of the London University Examinations by several pupils dirut from the Schools at which special classes are held, (free) fft pupils preparing for these examinations. Cambridge Locals 1. Twenty-six Certificates. College of Preceptors j Dec 1894. Fifty Certificates. SECRETARY: T. BREW'S, Esq., Solicitor.</p>
