        <p>Where to Go for my Holidays? This is a question which is now occupying the atten Lion of hundreds of our readers. Now the various health resorts of thr.• British Islands, as well as the Con- tent, will be shortly flocked with visitors. Second only m importance to Where to go to ? U, indeed, second to that is its natured corollary : How shall I de- rive the most benefit from my holiday? Now, any ex p rieciced medical min will tell you tha a course of soine suitable tonic medicine taken during the change will double the beneficial effects of the holi- day. The appetite for food will be sharpened. the as- similating powers of the stomach will be increased, the nervous system will be strengthened, the blood will be purified, and the indispensable "tone "regained by the system, mucu more certainty and effectually by such ,a course of medicine taken during the holiday alone or by the medicine alone. Each helps the other, and the ex- perienced in these matters always take both together. Great care, however, mast he exercised in the choice af your tonic. Many so-called remedies are absolutely injurious. There, is, however, one which long and uni- versal experience proves to be absolutely trustworthy, that can do no harm to the most delicate constitution, and has practically in every instance where it has been tried, evc a proved to be most beneficial, and, indeed, the most suitable tonic medicine for all such cases. This is the well-known preparation known as G wilym Evans' Quinine Bitters. THE VEGEJABLE TONIC. WHAT ARE ITS EFFECTS? 1. It assists and promotes Digestion. 2. It strengthens the Nerves and Muscles. 3. It Cleanses and Purifies the Blood. 4. It Enlivens the Spirits. 5. It removes all Obstructions and Impurities from the human body. 6. It gives Tone to the whole system. Sold in Bottles at is. lid., 2s. 9d., and 4s. 6d. each. Beware of Imitations! See the name of , Gwilynt Evans" on Label, Stamp, and Bottle.</p>
