      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-09-28_WidnesExaminer_art0093" n="art0093">
        <head>RUNCORN V. ROCHDALE HORNETS.</head>
        <p>RUNCORN V. ROCHDALE HORNETS.</p>
        <p>• - The Runcorn team inflicted a s.vere defeat on their oi`nonenta a: Runcorn on SOlarday. There wag a good number of Tectators to witness the m itch. In thr g y ab.enre of CI Robinsnn in the Roncnr, team, a trial was Et given to W-st-, a very nrorniaing *. A" teatner. Th fnllowin wa the order e k nI the players :—Rtinnorn : But- terwnrtit, ND hark • Dunh4vin, Myers, Warier, anti Wet. threr-quarter 17),icka ; S. Abrams and J. Faulkver, ivilf-hana ; W. Flolkner. F irnvrt Langley. Ligittfoltt Walker, Johnson, C. Pendiebury, t.nd H. Williams, for. wsrds. Roriviale Florttettt : W. Hire, back ; Atkinann. Fleteher, Mslledew and Lorkamith,three-goarter harks; Maarin and Orden. 1„,ir..t,,,,.ks ; niggina, Trevor, flill, Lrach, R -•°thwell, Kershaw, Turner, and Dearden, for- wards. . A start svaa eff,cte,4 at 3 40. Runcorn wirinina the to•a, the Hornets had to face sun and wind. Higgins kicked off- Play was even for some minutes at centre. until the Riiiwywn forwards got going. A free kick paved the Hornets' side from disaster. A minute later Rigg was applauded for a fine catch from a punt by Farmer. ' Runcorn again got down, and the Hornets were pena- -</p>
